# Canvas Project Defaults

- Keep diffs small and local; do not refactor unrelated parts of the file.
- Prefer existing vanilla HTML, CSS, and browser APIs over new dependencies or build tooling.
- Treat `canvas.html` as the primary app surface; only split code into new files when it clearly reduces complexity.
- Preserve current UI behavior unless the task explicitly asks for a behavior change.
- Reuse existing naming, DOM patterns, and state structure before introducing new helpers.
- Add comments only for non-obvious constraints, tradeoffs, or browser gotchas.
